      "raw": "<p>Jackhandle rewrites the targetting of the attack, it doesn&#39;t actually cancel the original attack, just alters the wording of it. &nbsp;At least that is my understanding.</p><p>With Jackhandle Strike becomes deal all non-hero targets 1 melee damage, so I would appy it to the whole thing the same as Squall.</p><p>Crowbar responds to damage Mr. Fixer deals by then hitting a different target for the same amount (+ modifiers)</p><p>Crowbars + Strike + Living Weapon should result in (1+2+1) 4 melee, and then (4+1) 5 melee.</p><p>It should not gain the effect of Living Weapon on the second hit anymore than Cosmic&#39;s Autonomous Blade should if you had that on Fixer and used strike. &nbsp;They both respond to damage being dealt.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Thinking this through the Video Game resolution of Crowbars + Jackhandle makes sense to me, as Jackhandle is changing the targetting of Crowbars&#39; damage from &quot;he may deal that damge to one other target as well&quot; to &quot;he may deal that damage to all non-hero targets as well&quot;</p><p>Although following that logic it would seem that Crowbars should only respond once to damage dealt by Squall (if Guise borrowed crowbars and used Squall)</p><p>We will have to wait and see.</p><p>Either way once they sort out exactly how they want it to work I really hope we can get errata for it. &nbsp;If not printed at least posted and changed in the Video Game.</p>",
